      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-01-28_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <p>THE BOTRLHR GRAMMAR SCROOL, WARRINGTON. OLD BOYS' DINNER. The Third Annual Dinner will be held at the LION HOiltb, BRIDGE STREET. WARRING VON, ON TUESDAY EVRNING, THE 31ST JANUARY. 1905 at 7.30 prompt. President: Robert Pierpoint. Esq , M.P. Past Presidents : Jno. Whitt, Esq , J.P.; E. R. Pickmere, Req. M.A. Tickets, price 511. each (exclusive of wine), can be obtained from myself or from the undermentioned members ot the committee —Chas. S Burgesb J.P., Winmarleigh street ; Robson J. Chorley,Appleton , Robert Dobson,Golden square; begar Owen, Appleton ; Chas. D. Parkinson. Bewsev Chamber.; Arthur S. Wright, Wilson-Patten street ; J. Guest Gornall, M.D. Latchford ; Wm. Ernest Atkin. Bold street ; Edward A. White, Cairo street ; Stanley Walker, 29. Wilson- Patten street.- •Reeeption, 7to 7.30 p.m. during which time the Record Book will be open for signatures.—Rule 9 : " Itvtry Old Boy shall be eiritied to an invitation to the annual dinner."—JAMES HENRY SMErttURST, Hon. Sec.,lßriery emit, Warrington.' aggilk:</p>
      </div>
