      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-01-28_WidnesExaminer_art0003" n="art0003">
        <p>No. 1345 ONE PENNY"</p>
        <p>CHESHIRE COUNTY COUNCIL SCHOLARSHIPS. —THE EDUCATION COMMITTEE OFFERS FOR COMPETITION the following Scholarships : (a) A NUMBER TENABLE for 12 WEEKS at the DIARY INSTITUTE, Worleaton, for inatructi9n in Dairy Work, and commencing on Monday, February 27th neat. Applications for the same to be forwarded not later than February 13th, 1905.</p>
        <p>(b) ONE HUNDRED and FIFTY COUNTY JUNIOR SCHOLARSHIPS open to boys and mitts of not more than 14 years of age on August let 1905, to enable them to proceed to Secondary Day Sihools fcr a period of three years. Applications fur these ,to be rec Jived not later than March let 1905.</p>
        <p>(c) TWENTY COUNTY JUNIOR SCHOLARSHIPS to boy and girl 4 of 14 years ot age and upwards on August Ist 1905, who have ben in attendance at a Socondary School for at least two years and desire to become Pupil Teachers ar. the age of 16 or as soon after as possible. Apclizatirms tor these tu be received not later than Mao Ist. 1905.</p>
        <p>(d) TWO DAY SCHOLARSHIPS in ART SUBJECTS open to students of either sex who ate not less than 18 or more than 26 years of age on September Ist next, to enable them to pursue their studies for three ynars at the Royal School of Art, South Kensington. Applica- tions for these must be received not later than Marcia 31st, 1905. Particulars in regard to the above, and forms of application, can be obtained from RD. P. WARD,</p>
        <p>Directorof Educaiion, County EducationlOffioesVity:roadjChester.</p>
      </div>
