        <p>SILL RIGHTS RESERVED.]</p>
        <p>"You're very good," laughed Royce, " but when one hears that sort of thing from a total stranger, who cannot possibly desire to make another's' fellow's fortune out of pure benevo- knee, one—" " Naturally suspects him," interrupted the stranger. " I do not blame you. I may tell you, however, that I am acting merely as con- tideland agent. My principal is one whom you —and everyone else—know well, and whose mo- tives are above suspicion.. This distinguished gentleman has noted your name as one whom be would be ready to benefit in a, certain way which is his secret. If you care to learn in whose mane I am now speaking, I shall be pleased to inform you on receiving your word of honour that you will never under any circumstances whatever divulge it." " Well, I don't see what harm could come of my knowing that much, any way," laughed Royce. " Give mo your formal word that what I now you shall go sto farther." " Yes—l give it; I undertake to keep thiH knowledge a secret from all the world. hurt), ,slug that your communication proves to have bieli outdo bona fide, and that you have spoken the siuuiple ttuth.". .</p>
