      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-01-28_WidnesExaminer_art0124" n="art0124">
        <head>GRAPPENHALL</head>
        <p>GRAPPENHALL</p>
        <p>PRIMROSE LEAGI:E.—The Grappenhall Habitation of the Primrose League had a social gathering in the Large Room on January 20th. The evening's pro- gramme commenced with tea. The number present for tea was not great, but the concert which followed was very well attended. A pianoforte duet by Lady Croft and Miss Parr, songs by Miss Egerton Warburton, and Sir Archer Croft ; glees : and humourous sketches by Mr. H. Hallard, formed the items of the concert. Mr. Fearneley added political colour in his address. Mr. J. Charlton Parr occupied the chair, the Dame President, Mrs. Charlton Parr,also being present.</p>
        <p>Aa</p>
      </div>
