      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-01-28_WidnesExaminer_art0137" n="art0137">
        <head>FOR ENITORANTS.</head>
        <p>FOR ENITORANTS.</p>
        <p>I The handbook which has been issued by the Allan Line for the benefit of intending emigrants to Canada, or the United States is thoroughly up-to-date, and contains a great deal of practical information. Pre- faced by a concise and interesting outline of the largest and nearest of the British Colonies, the subjects treated in the score of pages embrace, "People who should Emigrate," "The Time to Emigrate," "How to cross the Atlantic," and "The Steamers of the Allan Line." In connection with the latter there are a number of excellent illustrations, including the now turbine steamers Victorian and Virgiffian, with a stern view of the former before launching, showing the triple propeller; and the ! Bavarian and Tunisian, together with pictures of the interiors of the vessels. Useful advice is also afforded as to what emigrants should take with them in the way of clothing and household necessaries, and sp+ial refer- ence is made to the question of luggage and many other important matters. The Allan Line is to be congratu- lated on the notable success of their past year's working the number of emigrants carried forming a record in the history of the line, but there is every reason to believe that this total vill be eclipsed during the year which has just opened, in view of the advent of the new turbine steamers.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-01-28_WidnesExaminer_art0138" n="art0138">
        <head>HOW THE LUNGS BECOME DISEASED.</head>
        <p>HOW THE LUNGS BECOME DISEASED.</p>
        <p>IT IS THE HAWKING AND COUGHING- THAT DESTROYS THE TISSUES OF THE LUNGS,</p>
        <p>AND MAKES THESt WEAK AND SORE.</p>
        <p>IWhat you want is something to stop the hawking and takes the soreness out of the throat and chest. Nothing compares with VENWS LIGHTNING COUGH CURE ; it 'soothes inflAmed membranes, eradicates the catarrhal nuiscus ; you feel well quickly. For weak lungs !catarrh, bronchitis, chronic coughs and throat trouble Ithere is no remedy to be compared with VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH dUILFI. Relief comes Instantly, and a permanent cure follows. It is strongly recommended by such Englishmen as %V. Istscelles Scott, F.R.M.S., Granville H. Sharpe, F.C.S.. Re r. W. W. Tulloch, D.D. !Ask for VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE, 9d. is. land 21. 9d. at Chemists everywhere.</p>
